 "equations": [],
 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Use",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Application: signals in low-voltage, high-frequency circuits. Listed features: low turn-on voltage and fast switching."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Temperature and derating",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Full 200 mW dissipation is allowed up to 25 °C ambient; above that the limit falls in a straight line to zero at 125 °C. Typical reverse current from 0 to 40 V is about 5 to 32 nA at 100 °C, against about 0.06 to 0.5 nA at 25 °C."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Capacitance",
   "page": 2,
   "text": "Terminal capacitance falls with reverse bias, from about 15 pF at 0 V to under 3 pF near 20 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Construction and handling",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Moisture sensitivity level 1 per J-STD-020, lead-free reflow peak 260 °C. The molding compound is UL 94V-0 rated, RoHS-compliant and halogen-free. Leads are solder plated and solderable per MIL-STD-750, Method 2026. A band on the body marks the cathode end."
  }
 ],
